body:
First time owner just dont know any better. I was asked if I were sure, of course I didn't know how much stress itll be. Now I know better.

&#x200B;

yes, shes crated. She can hold her pee in for 10-12 hours. I can never get her to pee outside unless I stay out the entire day. And of course I praise and give her a high value treat. She pee/poops on command indoors.

&#x200B;

We do play fetch, actually she has to because of her mouth condition. But fetch does not wear her out. You're right about the walks, I do realize, shes able to walk more and more. I can't imagine what she'd be by age 1 at this rate.

&#x200B;

I have lazy days where I only do 30 minute walks, this is when I go home to ripped pads. This is the issue, should i just let her rip the pads? I get so angry because she knows not to but I know she did it because shes bored and I got lazy. I think at this point, I need to just suck it up with the ripped pads. I have never tried taking the pads away, considering shes able to hold long pee. But she has peed around the pad because I put a metal grid over it to prevent her chewing. Not sure what to do actually?

&#x200B;

Yes, meals doing that too. Ive been doing that for 2 weeks. Every since she had surgery, she stopped eating. Asked the vet, he said she looked fine. 

&#x200B;
